description: Supabase Postgres migration and schema rules
globs: supabase/**
alwaysApply: false
---

# Database (supabase/)

- Migrations are append-only: add a NEW timestamped file
  (`supabase migration new <name>` -> `supabase/migrations/<YYYYMMDDHHMMSS>_<name>.sql`).
  Never edit a migration that has been applied or merged.
- Phase 0 migrations are frozen; schema changes go through the integrator.
- Every tenant-owned table has `tenant_id` and every query filters by it.
- Enable RLS on every table (no policies = no access for anon/authenticated roles).
- Money columns are `numeric(18,6)`; never `float`/`real`/`double precision`.
- `supabase/seed.sql` is generated by `scripts/generate_seed.py` (Workstream D).
- Apply locally with `make db-reset` (destructive). Never run it against shared data
  without asking.
